<!-- ============ 01 · THE COVER ============ -->
<header class="cover" aria-labelledby="h1">
  <p class="ghost-book" aria-hidden="true">Book</p>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="mast"><span>Straw Dogs Development <b>·</b> Books for speakers, founders and experts</span><span class="issue">American Fork, Utah · 2026</span></p>
    <div class="cover-grid">
      <div class="cover-copy">
        <h1 id="h1">Your name goes on the cover. <em>Make it the book that moves people.</em></h1>
        <p class="cover-sub">Straw Dogs builds books for speakers, founders and experts that move readers to act, fill speaking calendars, and open doors. Over thirty titles. The two people you meet are the two who write it.</p>
        <div class="cover-ctas">
          <a class="btn" href="#engage">Talk about your book <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="tlink" href="#work">See the books we’ve built ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fan-wrap">
        <div class="fan">
          <img class="b1" src="/images/covers/life-is-luck.webp" alt="Life is Luck by John Morgan" width="320" height="460" loading="eager">
          <img class="b2" src="/images/covers/stupider-people.webp" alt="Stupider People Have Done It by Jay Schwedelson" width="303" height="460" loading="eager">
          <img class="f1" src="/images/covers/daymakers.webp" alt="The Daymaker Difference by Jay O’Brien and Jeff Jackel" width="307" height="441" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
          <span class="fan-cap" aria-hidden="true">On the cover · 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="lines" aria-label="In this issue">
        <li><span class="cl-a">#1 on Amazon, three categories</span><span class="cl-b">The Daymaker Difference</span></li>
        <li><span class="cl-a">Over thirty titles</span><span class="cl-b">Lisa Nichols · John Morgan · FranklinCovey</span></li>
        <li><span class="cl-a">Page to screen</span><span class="cl-b">The Best Christmas Pageant Ever · Lionsgate, 2024</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============ 02 · COVER STORIES ============ -->
<section class="section tint" id="stories" aria-label="Cover stories">
  <div class="folio" aria-hidden="true"><div class="wrap"><span>02 · Cover stories</span><span>The Daymaker Difference · Stupider People Have Done It</span></div></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="spread">
      <div class="dm-stage">
        <img class="dm-photo" src="/images/platte-number-one.webp" alt="Platte F. Clark smiling and holding up one finger" width="1400" height="1447" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="thread" role="group" aria-label="Text message from the authors">
          <p class="from">Jeff Jackel · co-author</p>
          <p class="bubble in">Platte! We did it!! We’re #1 in all three categories!!!</p>
          <p class="bubble out">That’s awesome! Congrats!!</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gutter" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="dm-copy">
        <p class="kicker rv"><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>Cover story · #1 on Amazon</p>
        <h2 class="h2 rv">Number one, <span class="turn">three times over.</span></h2>
        <p class="dropcap">Jay O’Brien and Jeff Jackel built Client Giant on the conviction that caring for customers is a profit strategy, not a soft skill. The book had to make that case to readers who measure everything. In launch week it took the top spot in three Amazon categories at once.</p>
        <ol class="ledger" aria-label="Amazon rankings at launch">
          <li><span class="no">#1</span><span class="cat">Marketing</span><span class="lst">New Releases</span></li>
          <li><span class="no">#1</span><span class="cat">Sales &amp; Selling</span><span class="lst">New Releases</span></li>
          <li><span class="no">#1</span><span class="cat">Customer Relations</span><span class="lst">Best Sellers</span></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="bookline">
          <img src="/images/covers/daymakers.webp" alt="The Daymaker Difference book cover" width="307" height="441" loading="lazy">
          <div>
            <p class="t">The Daymaker Difference</p>
            <p class="s">The Surprisingly Profitable Practice of Caring</p>
            <p class="w">Jay O’Brien &amp; Jeff Jackel · Co-founders, Client Giant</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="second">
      <figure class="jay-photo">
        <img src="/images/platte-jay.webp" alt="Platte F. Clark with Jay Schwedelson" width="900" height="1116" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption>On location · Jay Schwedelson &amp; Platte F. Clark</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="jay-copy">
        <p class="kicker rv">Also in this issue · #1 Bestseller</p>
        <h3 class="rv">Stupider People <span class="turn">Have Done It</span></h3>
        <p class="who">Jay Schwedelson · <i>Stupider People Have Done It</i></p>
        <p class="sub">Marketing truths, career moves, and life advice for doers.</p>
        <p class="body">Schwedelson built one of the largest email-marketing voices on the internet without ever sounding like one. The book had to do the same on the page—direct, funny, generous, and structured so a reader can run with it the next morning.</p>
        <div class="outnow">
          <img src="/images/covers/stupider-people.webp" alt="Stupider People Have Done It book cover" width="303" height="460" loading="lazy">
          <div><p class="l">Out Now · 2026</p><p class="n">Available wherever you buy books.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 03 · IN THEIR WORDS (the reel) ============ -->
<section class="section reel" id="words" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Client quotes">
  <div class="folio" aria-hidden="true"><div class="wrap"><span>03 · In their words</span><span>Four authors, four books</span></div></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker reel-head rv">In their words</p>
    <div class="slides" id="slides" aria-live="off">
      <figure class="slide is-active" id="q1" role="tabpanel" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="1 of 4: Lisa Nichols">
        <p class="gname" aria-hidden="true">Lisa</p>
        <figure class="polaroid">
          <img src="/images/lisa-platte-houston.webp" alt="Lisa Nichols and Platte F. Clark on stage at Speak &amp; Write in Houston" width="1085" height="1355" loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Speak &amp; Write · Houston</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <blockquote>“One of the best‑kept secrets in the <em>highest demand</em>.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption>
          <img src="/images/covers/becoming-unforgettable.webp" alt="" width="307" height="460" loading="lazy">
          <span><span class="nm">Lisa Nichols</span><span class="ln">Featured in The Secret and on Oprah</span></span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="slide" id="q2" role="tabpanel" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="2 of 4: Jason Stacy">
        <p class="gname" aria-hidden="true">Jason</p>
        <blockquote>“Platte didn’t just help with my ideas. He <em>created some</em> that fit perfectly into what I do.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption>
          <img src="/images/covers/pressure-code.webp" alt="" width="309" height="460" loading="lazy">
          <span><span class="nm">Jason Stacy</span><span class="ln">Performance coach to Aryna Sabalenka</span></span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="slide" id="q3" role="tabpanel" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="3 of 4: Jay Schwedelson">
        <p class="gname" aria-hidden="true">Jay</p>
        <blockquote>“Platte really nailed it, which is no small feat ’cause I handed him <em>a bit of chaos</em>.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption>
          <img src="/images/covers/stupider-people.webp" alt="" width="303" height="460" loading="lazy">
          <span><span class="nm">Jay Schwedelson</span><span class="ln">Stupider People Have Done It</span></span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="slide" id="q4" role="tabpanel" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="4 of 4: Luke Falk">
        <p class="gname" aria-hidden="true">Luke</p>
        <blockquote>“If you’re looking to write a book, <em>call Platte</em>. He’ll show you how to elevate it that much more.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption>
          <img src="/images/covers/mind-strength.webp" alt="" width="307" height="460" loading="lazy">
          <span><span class="nm">Luke Falk</span><span class="ln">Former NFL quarterback</span></span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a quote">
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="t1" aria-controls="q1" aria-selected="true"><b>01</b>Lisa<span class="track"><span class="fill"></span></span></button>
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="t2" aria-controls="q2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><b>02</b>Jason<span class="track"><span class="fill"></span></span></button>
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="t3" aria-controls="q3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><b>03</b>Jay<span class="track"><span class="fill"></span></span></button>
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="t4" aria-controls="q4" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><b>04</b>Luke<span class="track"><span class="fill"></span></span></button>
      </div>
      <button class="pause" type="button" id="pause" aria-pressed="false"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="1" width="3" height="10"/><rect x="7" y="1" width="3" height="10"/></svg><span>Pause</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="reel-cta"><a class="tlink" href="#engage">Talk about your book →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

