      <p class="kicker rv">In this issue · What we build</p>
      <h2 class="h2 rv" id="build-h">Three things most ghostwriting firms <span class="turn">can’t do.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">Books are platforms, not endpoints.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div><h3 class="h3">Last-Mile Book Rescue</h3><p class="rsub">For 80%-complete manuscripts that aren’t landing.</p></div>
        <p class="body">You don’t need a full ghostwriter. You have a manuscript that’s eighty percent there—drafted by you, a coauthor, or an AI that reads like one. We diagnose what’s wrong (missing argument, broken character logic, no felt stakes) and rebuild what isn’t earning the page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull">
        <p>Specialist, not generalist. <span>Embedded, not networked.</span></p>
        <p class="fine">Most firms operate on a generalist-plus-network model. A salesperson signs you. A project manager checks in. A contracted writer you’ll never speak to drafts your book. <strong>The people you meet at the beginning are the people who write the book.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div><h3 class="h3">Page to Screen</h3><p class="rsub">For books with a film or series future.</p></div>
        <p class="body">Platte is a credited screenwriter on Lionsgate’s <i>The Best Christmas Pageant Ever</i> (2024 · 92% Critics / 97% Audiences), with film representation through Plain Text Talent. Authors with a film or series future engage us at the architecture stage—so the book is built for adaptation and positioned for the right Hollywood ear.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div><h3 class="h3">Curriculum &amp; Productization</h3><p class="rsub">Tools that transform organizations.</p></div>
        <p class="body">Three decades of curriculum design for FranklinCovey, VitalSmarts (Crucial Conversations), and ZengerFolkman—programs delivered to millions across six continents. When your book leads to a workshop, cohort program, assessment, or course, the architect of the book is the architect of the curriculum. No handoff.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

